+# Spec Delta: Populate grpc.lb.backend_service in subchannel metrics
+
+Status: implemented
+
+## Objective
+Per gRFC A94, subchannel OTel metrics carry `grpc.lb.backend_service` and
+`grpc.lb.locality` labels, set per endpoint by the cds LB policy. Today the
+backend_service label is always empty.
+
+## Current Behavior
+- `InternalSubchannel` reads `NameResolver.ATTR_BACKEND_SERVICE` from the
+  *EAG* attributes. That key is a `@ResolutionResultAttr` and is only set on the
+  resolution-result attributes (by `ClusterImplLoadBalancer`), never on EAGs.
+- `CdsLoadBalancer2` sets `EquivalentAddressGroup.ATTR_LOCALITY_NAME` on each
+  EAG, but nothing for the backend service.
+
+## New Behavior
+- New EAG-level key `EquivalentAddressGroup.ATTR_BACKEND_SERVICE` (String).
+- `CdsLoadBalancer2` sets it to the (leaf) cluster name on every endpoint EAG,
+  next to `ATTR_LOCALITY_NAME`.
+- `InternalSubchannel` reads `EquivalentAddressGroup.ATTR_BACKEND_SERVICE`
+  for the connection_attempts_succeeded/failed and disconnections metrics.
+
+## Success Criteria
+- CDS-produced EAGs carry `ATTR_BACKEND_SERVICE == clusterName`.
+- InternalSubchannel metrics report the backend service from the EAG attribute.
+- `NameResolver.ATTR_BACKEND_SERVICE` on resolution attributes is unchanged
+  (WRR still consumes it); existing tests pass.
+
+## Boundaries
+- Do not move the ClusterImpl ATTR_BACKEND_SERVICE code (tracked in #12431).
